6. Roles in a Web Project
In a typical web development project, the core roles involve distinct responsibilities:
•	Frontend Developer:
o	Focus: Implementing the visual and interactive elements of a website.
o	Responsibilities: Translating UI/UX design wireframes into functional HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code. Ensuring responsive design across various devices. Optimizing client-side performance.
•	Backend Developer:
o	Focus: Building and maintaining the core server-side logic, data access, and API (Application Programming Interface) creation.
o	Responsibilities: Writing application logic, handling user authentication and authorization, managing server-side security, and integrating with the database.
•	Database Administrator (DBA):
o	Focus: Designing, implementing, maintaining, and repairing an organization's databases.
o	Responsibilities: Ensuring data security and integrity, performance tuning of database queries, managing backups and recovery plans, and ensuring the database schema is efficient for the application's needs.
