7. VS Code Installation and Configuration
This step involves actions external to this text-based AI environment (installation and taking a screenshot).
General Steps to Install and Configure VS Code:
1.	Installation: Download the appropriate installer for your OS (Windows, macOS, or Linux) from the official Visual Studio Code website and follow the installation prompts.
2.	Configuration for Web Development: Once installed, open VS Code and install the following recommended extensions from the Extensions view (Ctrl+Shift+X or Cmd+Shift+X):
o	HTML, CSS, JavaScript Support: These are mostly built-in, but extensions can enhance them.
o	Live Server: Provides a quick way to launch a local development server for your HTML files with live-reloading.
o	Prettier - Code formatter: Automatically formats your HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code to maintain consistent style.
o	ESLint (for JavaScript): Analyzes code to find potential errors and enforce code style rules.
